    "kicker": "The main event",
    "title": "Fri 11/13 · Cooler PPI, but chips slide again",
    "body": "October PPI rose **0.3%** m/m, cooler than the 0.4% expected (core 0.3% as expected), but it is up 6.5% from a year ago and markets still price a December hike at about **89%**. Stocks slipped as HSBC downgraded Nvidia and chips sold off: S&P −0.4%, Nasdaq −0.9%, Dow +0.1%. The S&P still gained **2.5%** for the week, its first weekly gain since early October. The 10-year ended near **5.15%**. Next week: Nvidia reports Tue 11/17 after the close, its first quarter without Jensen Huang, and Anthropic aims to start trading Thu 11/19."
  },
