      "title": "FAA halts all US departures.",
      "body": "The FAA ordered a nationwide ground stop at 3:54p ET Friday after a telecommunications outage hit all Air Route Traffic Control Centers, according to Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy; departing flights were held until further notice. Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin said there was no sign so far of an attack. It is the first nationwide ground stop since January 2023. Airlines slipped into the close: United −1.7%, American −1.0%, Southwest −0.6%, Delta −0.4%. When flights resume was not confirmed as of Friday evening; watch airline stocks Monday."
