    {
      "title": "Oil flat; IEA sees first surplus since the Iran war.",
      "body": "WTI settled −0.2% at $88.56 and Brent +$0.02 at $95.84 Friday, after Thursday's jump on Trump saying the US doesn't need a deal with Iran. Brent posted a second weekly decline. The IEA said the market will be in surplus this quarter for the first time since the war began, as high prices weigh on demand. Shipping risk remains: Verisk Maplecroft counted 36 confirmed attacks on commercial ships around the Gulf and Hormuz in October, the most since the war began, and more ships were hit this week."
